{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547874-we-have-nosferatu-we-have-nosferatu-today","id":1547874,"title":"We have nosferatu, we have nosferatu today","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-21T05:06:00-08:00","id":1547874,"title":"We have nosferatu, we have nosferatu today","content":"(Anyone who can tell me where that title came from and why it\u2019s not actually appropriate to the actual subject of this thread wins bragging rights for at least the next five and possibly even ten minutes minutes).<br /> <br /> <br /> Fellow fans, as I\u2019m sure you\u2019re already aware a new Graf Orlock is growling, prowling and tearing his way through the streets of Wisborg, Germany (Not to mention residents thereof), and across cinema screens worldwide.<br /> <br /> Now given that this character is the namesake of Clan Nosferatu, one of the pillars of the Masquerade, it seems appropriate to ask \u201cWhat should THE Nosferatu look like in VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE terms?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> - For example, should he be a fully paid-up member of the eponymous Clan? (Especially in his newest incarnation, one could make a case for his being an unsociable Tzimisce).<br /> <br /> <br /> - When inserting Grak Orlock into Earth-Masquerade\u2019s backstory should we go with the classic \u2018Not Dracula, especially if Mrs Florence Stoker comes asking\u2019 storyline or should we go with THE SHADOW OF THE VAMPIRE storyline? (Which depicts the original NOSFERATU being filmed with an actual vampire passing himself off as \u2018Max Shreck\u2019, with carnage ensuing).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Finally, how old and of what generation should Graf Orlock be? (Are there any vampires in the Classic World of Darkness who would make an especially appropriate site for this very notorious vampire?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T05:11:49-08:00","id":1547875,"title":"","content":"Actually, one might also add \u201cWhat does the former Hanseatic port of Wisborg, somewhere on the German coast*, look like in Modern nights?\u201d<br /> <br /> For the record, it amuses me to imagine that the city itself would be almost empty of Nosferatu, but that the Clan would keep a \u2018listening post\u2019 in the surrounding region, apparently nervous as cats on the roof of a burning kennel about something in (or something that happened in) the city.<br /> <br /> Whether that would be a past humiliation or a current peril remains to be determined.<br /> <br /> <br /> *It seems fair to note that while the city appears to be inspired by Whitby (from DRACULA), a North Sea port, the original filming location was Wismar (A port on the Baltic Sea).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T16:30:35-08:00","id":1547883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547874-we-have-nosferatu-we-have-nosferatu-today?p=1547875#post1547875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, one might also add \u201cWhat does the former Hanseatic port of Wisborg, somewhere on the German coast*, look like in Modern nights?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably pretty quiet, Kindred-wise. Wismar's got less than 50,000 people, so it is probably too small to meet the conservative 1:100K ratio and would only have one or two Kindred by more generous ratios. Even Rostock, the largest city/port in Mecklenburg, is only 200,000 people, so you'd have 2-10, depending on your ratio.<br /> <br /> Now, Graf Orlok probably came to Germany once Dracula got too powerful and dominated the same region. Who knows, maybe the 1922 film was a psyop to deflect attention from Dracula to an old rival of his!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T16:57:43-08:00","id":1547884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547874-we-have-nosferatu-we-have-nosferatu-today#post1547874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (Anyone who can tell me where that title came from and why it\u2019s not actually appropriate to the actual subject of this thread wins bragging rights for at least the next five and possibly even ten minutes minutes).</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's from the twenties novelty song, &quot;Yes, We have no Bananas.&quot; It was made and released at a time when the main cultivar of bananas had been wiped out by a fungal disease and a banana shortage hit the United States.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547874-we-have-nosferatu-we-have-nosferatu-today#post1547874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now given that this character is the namesake of Clan Nosferatu, one of the pillars of the Masquerade, it seems appropriate to ask \u201cWhat should THE Nosferatu look like in VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE terms?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>While the Nosferatu clan has departed from its obvious inspiration in that neither the 1922 or 1977 movie main characters can probably qualify as being a member of its eponynous clan, I believe the answer is 1) yes, they must obviously be from that clan, and 2) if they can't, your gaming group is probably running the clan wrong. I certainly loved the Joshua Timbrook illustrations of the clan, and appreciate much of what was written in the original corebook and clanbook, but somewhere along the way the train ran off the railroad, and we all need to put it back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547874-we-have-nosferatu-we-have-nosferatu-today#post1547874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- When inserting Grak Orlock into Earth-Masquerade\u2019s backstory should we go with the classic \u2018Not Dracula, especially if Mrs Florence Stoker comes asking\u2019 storyline or should we go with THE SHADOW OF THE VAMPIRE storyline? (Which depicts the original NOSFERATU being filmed with an actual vampire passing himself off as \u2018Max Shreck\u2019, with carnage ensuing).</div> </div> </div> </div>I extensively prepped a planned chronicle set in interwar Berlin (1919-1939), and my intentions were to use the story as &quot;revealed&quot; in Shadow of the Vampire as inspiration if not in details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547874-we-have-nosferatu-we-have-nosferatu-today#post1547874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Finally, how old and of what generation should Graf Orlock be? (Are there any vampires in the Classic World of Darkness who would make an especially appropriate site for this very notorious vampire?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make him analogous to historical Count Dracula so around 500 years old. I'd default him to around 8th generation or 7th generation if I wanted him to be available to sire a PC who wanted maximum gen at the start.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T22:26:39-08:00","id":1547887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547874-we-have-nosferatu-we-have-nosferatu-today?p=1547884#post1547884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe it's from the twenties novelty song, &quot;Yes, We have no Bananas.&quot; It was made and released at a time when the main cultivar of bananas had been wiped out by a fungal disease and a banana shortage hit the United States.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as a reference, it appears in Dracula: Dead and Loving It, which presents Nosferatu as an occult book on vampires, and the movie is pretty thoroughly about a send up of an Old Clan Tzimisce member, not a Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-22T04:29:25-08:00","id":1547892,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> , you are correct, my good fan - incidentally, the film also has one of my very favourite Van Helsings (Played by Mel Brooks himself) and quite possibly the most \u2018Peak Harker\u2019 moment in all of cinema (When the Vampire Lucy fails to parlay her obvious charms into an evening meal because Jonathan Harker DOES NOT cheat on his fianc\u00e9e).<br /> <br /> Kudos to you!<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6423_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6423\" data-vbnamecard=\"6423\">higgipedia</a>, that was my impression of the likely situation vis a vis vampire population - I wonder if factoring in the population of the surrounding region (Presumably the German Baltic Sea coast, though part of me is tempted to make Wisborg a North Sea city as a tribute to the situation of Whitby) would help allow for a vampire population on the upper end of the range?<br /> <br /> Having said that, a regional vampire population of not much more than ten vampires would make Wisborg an excellent base of operations for a coterie, presumably as a \u2018starter\u2019 principality which they must defend against intruders and potential hostile takeovers.<br /> <br /> Also, if nothing else Graf Orlock meeting a sticky end in AD 1838 Germany might help explain why Count Dracula picked England as his home away from home \u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, May I please ask what you mean by \u2018running the Clan wrong\u2019? I\u2019m not very familiar with the twists and turns of Clan depictions and would be interested in seeing your own assessment.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also interested in learning more about your Interbellum Berlin campaign: might one please ask if you would be willing to share any details of that particular setting? (I know that the Prince of Berlin was horribly enthusiastic about the Nazi party, but little more than that).<br /> <br /> As for Graf Orlock, I wonder if it might be sensible to make his World of Darkness version somewhat older than the local Dracula - an established vampire in a position to look on with deep consternation as The Impaler basically tears up the rule book and goes his own bloody way (I wonder how one might introduce memory issues comparable to Mr Willem Dafoe\u2019s version of the character - some sort of injury? Simple isolation? Meddling by a more potent vampire?).<br /> <br /> It does seem appropriate to depict the character as a male \u2018Cleopatra\u2019 embraced for being too happy with his own good fortune (Presentable looks, aristocratic bloodline and record of achievement - possibly even scholarly achievements of the more occult kind).<br /> <br /> I wonder if a Carpathian Nosferatu would have the nerve to embrace an aristocrat from a bloodline associated with the Tzimisce?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-22T22:30:33-08:00","id":1547903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547874-we-have-nosferatu-we-have-nosferatu-today?p=1547892#post1547892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May I please ask what you mean by \u2018running the Clan wrong\u2019? I\u2019m not very familiar with the twists and turns of Clan depictions and would be interested in seeing your own assessment.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I mean is that the clan is now portrayed as aggressively gross and disgusting. They all live in sewers. They all stink. They all have swarms of insects living among them. And so on. That's fine for some members of the clan. But it is very far from Count Orlock and &quot;Dracula&quot; in the movies. The clan should be able to embrace their cinematic inspirations who are much less disgusting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547874-we-have-nosferatu-we-have-nosferatu-today?p=1547892#post1547892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m also interested in learning more about your Interbellum Berlin campaign: might one please ask if you would be willing to share any details of that particular setting? (I know that the Prince of Berlin was horribly enthusiastic about the Nazi party, but little more than that).</div> </div> </div> </div>It had absolutely nothing to do with the sourcebook Berlin By Night because I absolutely hated it. I only used a few (relatively minor) NPCs from it. I've had a long obsession with Weimar era Berlin and wanted to do it justice.<br /> <br /> In my (prepared, but never played) chronicle, the Ventrue Prince of Berlin (who was not Gustav Breidenstein, but a Dutch Ventrue who came to the city after the end of the Thirty Years War) was killed in early 1919. He was replaced with a female Toreador who ruled the city until the Gotterdamerung of 1945 which saw the city levelled and almost all native vampires destroyed. I planned to run the chronicle only until 1939 because I figured the players would not want to roleplay the agony of seeing the city destroyed (as well as avoid painful issues involving the Nazi Party during the war).<br /> <br /> The chronicle was tentatively titled &quot;Red Berlin&quot;. I still have all my materials and may run it some day, assuming I find players who really want to explore that period and place. It was originally intended as a twenty game session LARP (one game for every year) back when I was LARPing regularly, but that never got more than one page of notes. I later expanded that into a full blown tabletop chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547874-we-have-nosferatu-we-have-nosferatu-today?p=1547892#post1547892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if a Carpathian Nosferatu would have the nerve to embrace an aristocrat from a bloodline associated with the Tzimisce?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a valid choice. The Tzimisce were being destroyed from within by the Anarch Revolt at that time so other clans would take advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-26T15:26:46-08:00","id":1547963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547874-we-have-nosferatu-we-have-nosferatu-today?p=1547903#post1547903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I mean is that the clan is now portrayed as aggressively gross and disgusting. They all live in sewers. They all stink. They all have swarms of insects living among them. And so on. That's fine</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I agree with that. There seem to be far more well-dressed than disgusting Nosferatu in the recent books. Really only Felicia Page from <i>Let the Streets Run Red</i> and maybe Wauneka from <i>Chicago by Night V5</i> have the &quot;gross Nosferatu&quot; thing going.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Chicago by Night V5:</i></b><br /> <i>Cedrick Calhoun:</i> &quot;Cedrick is exceedingly dapper. Though his double-breasted suits and bowler hats evoke a different era, he brings a certain charm to the style. He\u2019s acquired quite the collection of pocket watches, and always has a chain peeking out from his vest.&quot; (p. 159)<br /> <i>Wauneka:</i> Wauneka\u2019s a solidly built guy who looks like he\u2019s mixed with a bit of everything: Native, African, Asian, Latino, you name it. He\u2019s the lump of rags and garbage lying inert in the mouth of an alleyway, huddled into the meager shelter of a door front, underneath a bench. His face, when it\u2019s not covered by a balaclava or concealed within the depths of his hoodie, is all ruined nose and protruding fangs, especially those that jut, tusk-like, from his lower jaw.&quot; (p. 161-162)<br /> <i>Edith Beaubien:</i> &quot;Most nights, Edith appears as the creature she is: tall, lean, and powerfully built with distinctive spiky bone spurs protruding from each vertebra and from the tips of her shoulders. She is bald and her unsettling acid-green eyes glow above sharp fangs that extend down past her red-glossed lips. Elaborate tattoos of lush vegetation \u2014 flowers, vines, trees, grasses, herbs, etc. \u2014 in screamingly vivid hues cover every visible inch of her skin. Because she takes great pride in her body art, she wears clothing that allows her ink to be seen.&quot; (p. 164)<br /> \u200b<i>Nathaniel Bordruff:</i> &quot;An enormously tall man in life, in undeath Nathaniel is a gaunt, cadaverous, praying [sic] mantis of a vampire, all unnaturally long limbs that look vaguely sharp at certain angles, a spindly stalk of a neck with a perfectly egg-shaped bald head atop it. He has lately taken to stealing plain black suits, white dress shirts, and black silk ties from big-and-tall men\u2019s apparel shops, in a doomed effort to look somewhat more presentable to potential human allies.&quot; (p. 166)<br /> <i>Rowan:</i> &quot;Rowan is 6\u20192\u201d and a lanky, beastly version of a vampire. Their ears and fingers come to points, their stomach sunken, ribs pronounced, eyes depressed, and skin rubbery. They are covered in tattoos and piercings from their mortal life. Rowan tends to wear genderqueer alternative-culture clothes like shiny black leggings and flower-print button-down shirts.&quot; (p. 171)<br /> <i>Adze:</i> &quot;Adze wears black round-rimmed glasses to hide the deformity of his blinded right eye. Adze takes great pride in his appearance, offsetting his Nosferatu features with crisp, tailored three-piece suits with contemporary African flourishes such as vests made of hand-woven kente or mudcloth.&quot; (p. 174)<br /> <br /> <i><b>The Chicago Folios:</b><br /> Martin: &quot;</i>Martin always goes smartly dressed in a variety of three-piece suits. His hands are hidden in leather gloves. High collars and wide hat brims obscure his face.&quot; (p. 133)<br /> <i>Salt:</i> &quot;Donning dark hoodies and cardigans, headphones, and a backpack, Salt could be any college student on any campus in Chicago. Her favorite sweater is a long black one with two large white X\u2019s screen-printed up the side.&quot; (p. 135)<br /> <br /> <b><i>Let the Streets Run Red:</i></b><br /> <i>Gabriella:</i> &quot;Gabriella wears oversized hoodies and often has a gaming headset over her ears. A glimpse at her face reveals the left half of it is covered in twisted scar tissue, with her left eyelid no longer functioning and all the hair on that side of her body apparently seared off. Her right side is flawless, her braided red hair draped down over her shoulder.&quot; (p. 195)<br /> <i>Felicia Page: </i>&quot;She has unhealed bullet holes in her chest and abdomen, through which cockroaches can often be seen crawling through her body. She has full control over the roaches\u2019 movement, and it amuses her to gross people out.&quot; (p. 197)<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-27T09:36:03-08:00","id":1547981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All I mean is that the clan is now portrayed as aggressively gross and disgusting. They all live in sewers. They all stink. They all have swarms of insects living among them. And so on. That's fine for some members of the clan. But it is very far from Count Orlock and &quot;Dracula&quot; in the movies. The clan should be able to embrace their cinematic inspirations who are much less disgusting. </div> </div> </div>Well, you know, except for the plague rats (and in all fairness, Dracula and Orlock live in partly-ruinous castles, rather than aristocratic comfort: the latter in particular seems to reside all alone, in the vicinity of a werewolf-haunted forest.<br /> <br /> On the other hand it\u2019s definitely not a sewer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that's a valid choice. The Tzimisce were being destroyed from within by the Anarch Revolt at that time so other clans would take advantage </div> </div> </div>.\u200b<br /> <br /> Cainite politics can be relied upon to default to what Sir Pterry Pratchett described as the \u2018Crab Bucket\u2019 approach - nobody gets out alive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}